course: dictionary
lesson: 10494
title: Proper nouns: the Tuscarora
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Tuscarora starts with a capital letter because it is a name. It names a people, a language and some places. A proper noun is the name of one particular person, place or group, so it always begins with a capital letter.
explain: Context helps you see what kind of name it is. «The Haudenosaunee Confederacy united the Mohawk, Oneida, Onondaga, Cayuga and Seneca, later the Tuscarora, under a Great Law of Peace.» The list shows the Tuscarora are a group of people, just like the nations before them, who joined later.
explain: One word can name more than one thing. «The Tuscarora language belongs to the Iroquoian family» means the language. A sentence about a town or a mountain area would mean a place. Ask yourself what the sentence is about before you decide which meaning fits.
fact: A proper noun is a name, and it begins with a capital letter, such as Tuscarora, Ontario or New York.
fact: The Tuscarora are a Native American people who lived in what is now North Carolina.
fact: Later, the Tuscarora moved north to New York and Ontario, Canada.
fact: Tuscarora is also the name of their language, which belongs to the Iroquoian family.
fact: In the 1720s the Tuscarora joined the Haudenosaunee (Iroquois) Confederacy, which made it the Six Nations.
exercise: Why does «Tuscarora» start with a capital letter? | Because it is always the first word of a sentence | Because it is written in a loud voice | *Because it is the name of a particular people | Because it is an important action word
exercise: «The Tuscarora moved north later.» Where did the Tuscarora move to, according to the entry? | Into a school | *To New York and Ontario, Canada | To the middle of a desert | Under the sea
exercise: «The Tuscarora language belongs to the Iroquoian family.» In this sentence, what does Tuscarora mean? | A kind of verb | *The language of the Tuscarora people | A mountain area | A town hall
test: In the 1720s, what did the Tuscarora join? | A football club | A railway company | *The Haudenosaunee (Iroquois) Confederacy | The Roman army
test: Besides a people, what else can the word Tuscarora name? | A colour and a bird | *A language and some places | A month of the year | Two verbs and a number
exam: In «The Tuscarora moved north», why is Tuscarora written with a capital T? | It is always the first word in a sentence | *It is a proper noun, the name of a people | It shows the word is being shouted | It is an important action word
